{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 13 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". Count sequences with no run of 3 identical bits. Classic Fibonacci-like. Count sequences of length n with no 3 consecutive equal bits. Let a_n be count. Recurrence: a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}. Actually for binary with no 3 consecutive same, we can use states: last run length and bit. Let's compute via DP.\n\nLet dp[n][k][b] where k=1 or 2 length of current run, b=0/1. Transition: from dp[n-1][k][b] to dp[n][k+1][b] if k<2; else to dp[n][1][1-b]. Base n=1: dp[1][1][0]=1, dp[1][1][1]=1. Compute up to n=13.\n\nLet's do quickly.\n\nn=1:\nk1,b0:1\nk1,b1:1\n\nn=2:\nFrom k1,b0: can extend same -> k2,b0:1 ; or switch -> k1,b1:1\nFrom k1,b1: extend -> k2,b1:1 ; switch -> k1,b0:1\nSo dp2:\nk1,b0:1 (from switch)\nk1,b1:1\nk2,b0:1\nk2,b1:1\n\nn=3:\nFrom k1,b0: extend -> k2,b0:1 ; switch -> k1,b1:1\nFrom k1,b1: extend -> k2,b1:1 ; switch -> k1,b0:1\nFrom k2,b0: cannot extend (would be 3) so switch -> k1,b1:1\nFrom k2,b1: switch -> k1,b0:1\nSum:\nk1,b0: from k1,b1 switch (1) + from k2,b1 switch (1) =2\nk1,b1: from k1,b0 switch (1)+ from k2,b0 switch (1)=2\nk2,b0: from k1,b0 extend (1)=1\nk2,b1: from k1,b1 extend (1)=1\n\nn=4:\nFrom k1,b0(2): extend->k2,b0:+2 ; switch->k1,b1:+2\nFrom k1,b1(2): extend->k2,b1:+2 ; switch->k1,b0:+2\nFrom k2,b0(1): switch->k1,b1:+1\nFrom k2,b1(1): switch->k1,b0:+1\nTotals:\nk1,b0: from k1,b1 switch 2 + from k2,b1 switch 1 =3\nk1,b1: from k1,b0 switch 2 + from k2,b0 switch 1 =3\nk2,b0: from k1,b0 extend 2 =2\nk2,b1: from k1,b1 extend 2 =2\n\nn=5:\nFrom k1,b0(3): extend->k2,b0:+3 ; switch->k1,b1:+3\nFrom k1,b1(3): extend->k2,b1:+3 ; switch->k1,b0:+3\nFrom k2,b0(2): switch->k1,b1:+2\nFrom k2,b1(2): switch->k1,b0:+2\nTotals:\nk1,b0: 3+2=5\nk1,b1"}}],"created":1790936737,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\mod